  "description": "meme-id: trans-sports; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a woman with visible tattoos and a confident posture, juxtaposed with the text 'trans-sports: allowing medicore male athletes to finally become champions.' This framing is intentionally derogatory and hateful, targeting transgender individuals by implying they are not legitimate athletes and by mocking the idea of 'male athletes' becoming champions through transition. The term 'medicore' is used pejoratively to demean the athletic ability of transgender athletes, suggesting they are only 'champions' because of their gender transition rather than their actual skill. This meme promotes harmful stereotypes and directly attacks transgender people based on their gender identity, fitting the definition of hateful content as it targets a protected characteristic (gender identity) with derogatory and discriminatory intent.",
